      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=(z-1)^{2}\\,?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{6} & =(z-1)^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =(z-1)^{2} \\\\ \\pm (x+1) & =z-1 \\\\ z & =\\pm (x+1)+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=-x$ and $z=x+2.$",
